      "text": "To solve the problem, we can use the relationship between pressure and volume for gases at constant temperature, which is described by Boyle's Law. Boyle's Law states that the pressure \\( P \\) of a gas is inversely proportional to its volume \\( V \\). This can be written mathematically as:\n\n\\[ P_1 V_1 = P_2 V_2 \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( P_1 \\) is the initial pressure,\n- \\( V_1 \\) is the initial volume,\n- \\( P_2 \\) is the final pressure,\n- \\( V_2 \\) is the final volume.\n\nGiven:\n- \\( P_1 = 5 \\) kPa,\n- \\( V_1 = 2.28 \\) liters,\n- \\( V_2 = 5.7 \\) liters.\n\nWe need to find \\( P_2 \\). Rearranging Boyle's Law to solve for \\( P_2 \\), we get:\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{P_1 V_1}{V_2} \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values into the equation:\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\times 2.28 \\, \\text{liters}}{5.7 \\, \\text{liters}} \\]\n\nNow, we perform the calculation step by step:\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{11.4 \\, \\text{kPa} \\cdot \\text{liters}}{5.7 \\, \\text{liters}} \\approx 2 \\, \\text{kPa} \\]\n\nTherefore, the new pressure is \\(\\boxed{2}\\) kPa.",
